title: RIP phase-4 proof — the checkout soak against a build that answers nothing
description: The soak's shape, twenty-four one-second windows, against the proof's hung service, with no thresholds declared. Every window is a blackout. A request may not wait longer than its window, so each window ends on its clock, none is skipped, the plan is not truncated and the run completes, with every window recorded as unanswered. The verdict for the build must then say it cannot be compared rather than call it unchanged.

tags[2]: proof, performance
kind: performance
target:
  system: checkout
  technology: http
  environment: demo

load:
  tool: oha
  script: http://127.0.0.1:44381/
  vus: 2
  duration_s: 24
  profile:
    type: soak
    sample_interval_s: 1

method[1]:
  - name: hold-for-the-soak
    activity_type: action
    provider:
      type: process
      path: sh
      arguments[2]: "-c", "sleep 25"
      timeout_s: 90.0

rollbacks[0]:
